                    {
                        "sense_id": "05fd4f14-bfbc-3fae-8207-ecb6c4994e13",
                        "entry_id": "af50467a-b1fc-3b36-a24a-9eafa255c07a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Divination par l’interprétation de l’apparence et du comportement des rats et des souris."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Anciennement"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8bd3e9a1-9740-495d-ae65-1b7823a39ef0",
                                "sense_id": "05fd4f14-bfbc-3fae-8207-ecb6c4994e13",
                                "text": "Les Grecs et les Romains eurent pour toutes ces sottises le respect le plus religieux, tant qu’ils ne furent point éclairés par la culture des sciences ; mais ils s’en désabusèrent peu à peu. Caton, consulté sur ce que pronostiquaient des bottines mangées par des rats, répondit qu'il n’y avait rien de surprenant en cela ; mais que c’eût été un prodige inouï si les bottines avaient mangé les rats. Cicéron ne fut pas plus crédule : la myomancie n’est pas mieux traitée dans ses livres, et il n’épargne pas le ridicule à toutes les autres sortes de divinations, sans en excepter ni les oracles, ni les augures, ni les aruspices."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1066310a-22ba-45b5-a884-80b47e8810f8",
                        "source_entry_id": "af50467a-b1fc-3b36-a24a-9eafa255c07a",
                        "source_sense_id": "05fd4f14-bfbc-3fae-8207-ecb6c4994e13",
                        "target_lang_word": "myomancy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "myomancy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8b52566e-b9b4-36a4-b947-9bf1f90c65f6",
                                        "entry_id": "5d78b037-80ad-37b0-ae34-b277056fefb7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Divination by interpreting rats or mice. Their cries were believed to indicate the presence of evil."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "615fe0b9-089c-43b8-9e7d-54d3e767ea1e",
                                                "sense_id": "8b52566e-b9b4-36a4-b947-9bf1f90c65f6",
                                                "text": "1855 Elihu Rich in Smedley et al. Occult Sci.\nMyomancy was a method of divination by rats and mice, and is supposed to be alluded to in Isaiah lxvi. 17. Their peculiar cries, or some marked devastation committed by them, was taken for a prognostic of evil."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a167625f-e407-4907-98a6-e44f40540627",
                                                "sense_id": "8b52566e-b9b4-36a4-b947-9bf1f90c65f6",
                                                "text": "Pliny has a chapter on myomancy, or soothsaying by means of rats and mince, (Nat. Hist., lib. ix. c. 57)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29b12d3e-59d9-4bc3-89e8-6c5c271488bd",
                                                "sense_id": "8b52566e-b9b4-36a4-b947-9bf1f90c65f6",
                                                "text": "1903 Daniels & Stevans Encyc. Occult Sci.\nMyomancy - Made use of the sounds and damage done by rats. The great Dictator Fabius Maximus renounced his throne when warned by the squeal of a mouse and Cassius Flaminius threw up his command of cavalry."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5765b372-1e43-4ccd-8200-b2fd06002a1a",
                                                "sense_id": "8b52566e-b9b4-36a4-b947-9bf1f90c65f6",
                                                "text": "Myomancy. Divination by mice or rats, for instance, rats leaving a sinking ship."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
